ORA-00312: online log string thread string: 'string' 
ORA-27037: unable to obtain file status 

-> the file not in the OS 
-> permission issues 
-> disk unmount 

ORA-00313 / 00312 / 27037 happens after a Clone:
When you clone a database (via RMAN duplicate, Data Pump, or manual copy), the controlfiles in the cloned database may still reference the redo log paths of the source database.

Example
Source DB redo log paths:
Redo Log  	Path
redo01.log	/u01/app/oracle/oradata/ORCL/redo01.log
redo02.log	/u01/app/oracle/oradata/ORCL/redo02.log

After cloning, if the server paths differ or don’t exist:
Oracle tries to open /u01/app/oracle/oradata/ORCL/redo01.log
Path may not exist → ORA-27037 (unable to obtain file status)
Oracle fails to open redo log → ORA-00313
ORA-00312 shows which redo log file / thread caused the problem

FIX: 

SELECT group#, status 
FROM v$log;  
--it shows CURRENT log, INACTIVE

SELECT group#, member FROM v$logfile; 

--you can drop  INACTIVE and refer to uncorrected path 
ALTER DATABASE DROP LOGFILE GROUP 7; 
ALTER DATABASE DROP LOGFILE GROUP 8; 
ALTER DATABASE DROP LOGFILE GROUP 9; 
